# The network of "The tunnel is down": the shop's office and its VPN
# gateway, the office's internet provider on its new line, the internet,
# and the cloud provider's VPN gateway with the shop's cloud network.
#
#   office --- vpn --- isp ==(the new line)== internet --- cloud --[vpc]-- app
#   192.168.10.10  198.51.100.10                        203.0.113.10   10.20.1.10
#
# vpn is the office's VPN gateway, the learner's. isp (the office's
# internet provider) and internet are routers that aren't the learner's:
# between them runs the provider's new line, whose links carry at most
# 1,400 bytes, and neither router sends "destination unreachable" (its
# firewall, below). cloud stands in for a cloud provider's VPN gateway (AS
# 64512) and isn't the learner's either.
machine office
machine vpn router
machine isp router
machine internet router
machine cloud router
machine app

link office:eth0=192.168.10.10/24 vpn:lan=192.168.10.1/24
link vpn:wan=198.51.100.10/24 isp:office=198.51.100.1/24
link isp:line=192.0.2.1/30 internet:line=192.0.2.2/30
link internet:cloud=203.0.113.1/24 cloud:wan=203.0.113.10/24
lan vpc cloud:vpc=10.20.0.1/16 app:eth0=10.20.1.10/16
route office default via 192.168.10.1
route app default via 10.20.0.1
route isp 203.0.113.0/24 via 192.0.2.2
route internet 198.51.100.0/24 via 192.0.2.1
mtu isp line 1400
mtu internet line 1400

# The provider's end of the tunnel. Key 7 is the mark that ties its vti0 to
# the IPsec SA whose mark_in and mark_out are 7 (cloud's swanctl file).
tunnel cloud vti0 vti local 203.0.113.10 remote 198.51.100.10 key 7 addr 169.254.21.1/30

run vpn frr strongswan nftables
run isp nftables
run internet nftables
run cloud frr strongswan
run app nginx web-svc
